Open work
=========

Validation
----------
- Validate official ITU/EBU conformance signals across supported rates and
  channel layouts; native-reference equality alone is not certification.
- Extend native GCC/MSVC/Linux, Intel Mac and hardware x64 validation.
  Check extended-precision/x87 rounding and x64 filter register pressure
  before enabling AArch64-style full stereo histories there.
- Measure sustained real music, other works and cold-storage performance.
  Conservative peak screening can add overhead on continuously loud signals.
- Validate real Windows ACL denials, sharing failures, SMB/cloud providers,
  case-sensitive NTFS and concurrent input replacement. Expand parser fuzzing.
- Evaluate the optional rate-aware dither through listening tests.

Implementation and maintenance
-------------------------------
- Encapsulate analysis/dither/RNG globals before library or parallel use;
  define deterministic album and RNG ordering first.
- Profile noise-shaped dither and further common-path specialization while
  preserving histories, RNG sequence and rounding.
- Evaluate further interpolation screening/data-layout changes using exact
  kernel and complete-output checks; preserve output peak verification.
- Clean up legacy non-UTF-8 license-comment encoding without altering notices.
  The existing Clang warning remains until that work is completed.
- Review outdated Debian packaging.

Keep current behavior in README and tests. Detailed investigations, timings,
JSON evidence and completed-work histories are maintained locally under the
ignored local-research/ directory; they are not distributed with the repository.
